1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
In high-stakes oncology and cardiovascular diagnosis, false negatives are catastrophic.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,800
When evaluating breast tumor biopsies or patient cardiac biomarker panels, classical machine learning algorithms—

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:15,500
from Random Forests to deep neural networks—frequently struggle to capture subtle, high-order non-linear correlations

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,000
without severely overfitting small patient cohorts.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,500
To resolve this bottleneck, we engineered QuantumHealth:

6
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:30,500
an end-to-end, production-grade hybrid quantum-classical machine learning framework.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,000
By mapping complex biological biomarker vectors into 2^N-dimensional quantum Hilbert spaces,

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,500
we expose diagnostic patterns that remain invisible to classical decision surfaces.

9
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Our platform is structured across three decoupled tiers.

10
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,000
In Tier 1, patient records undergo clinical imputation, outlier scaling, and PCA/Mutual Information reduction,

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
condensing biomarkers to 4 through 8 orthogonal features tailored for current Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum hardware.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
In Tier 2, our unified ModelFactory and QuantumBackendManager interface directly with PennyLane state-vector simulators.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
We formulate three quantum models: Quantum Support Vector Classifiers using quantum state fidelity kernels,

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Variational Quantum Classifiers trained via analytic parameter-shift gradients,

15
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:20,000
and Hybrid Quantum Neural Networks coupling PyTorch layers with quantum circuits.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Tier 3 delivers this computational engine to clinicians through an intuitive web dashboard and headless CLI.

17
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,000
Let's step into the live platform.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,500
The executive dashboard displays real-time telemetry across 872 clinical cohort samples and 7 benchmarked architectures.

19
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:41,000
Under Data Explorer, clinicians can profile the Wisconsin Diagnostic Breast Cancer and UCI Heart Disease datasets

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,500
with instant statistical profiling and interactive Plotly correlation matrices.

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:51,500
Navigating to Model Studio, training a quantum classifier requires zero terminal commands.

22
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,000
We select 4 qubits, 25 epochs, and click "Start Training".

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,500
Watch as PennyLane executes the parameter-shift optimization rule:

24
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:06,800
our live convergence curve plots real-time loss reduction as the variational angles align with the biological decision boundary,

25
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:11,500
achieving 96.5% test accuracy in just 4.1 seconds.

26
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Clinicians can immediately test single-patient inference, or open our Explainability studio.

27
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:21,500
Using model-agnostic KernelSHAP, the quantum black-box is completely demystified:

28
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:27,000
here, for Patient #42, we see exactly how nuclear concavity and perimeter accelerated the malignant probability to 91.4%,

29
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
providing immediate actionable evidence for attending oncologists.

30
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,500
In rigorous head-to-head empirical benchmarking against classical Support Vector Machines, Random Forests, XGBoost,

31
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:43,000
and Multi-Layer Perceptrons, our Quantum VQC and HQNN models achieved the highest overall diagnostic performance.

32
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:49,000
On the WDBC oncology cohort, VQC achieved a remarkable 0.9854 ROC-AUC and 96.49% accuracy,

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
outperforming classical RBF SVMs and tree ensembles.

34
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,500
Using non-parametric Wilcoxon signed-rank tests across 10-fold cross-validation folds,

35
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:05,000
this quantum advantage demonstrated statistical significance at p = 0.038, well below the standard 0.05 threshold.

36
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,500
Furthermore, training latency on standard CPU simulation remains under five seconds,

37
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:15,000
proving the computational practicality of our implementation.

38
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,500
QuantumHealth is fully containerized with Docker, covered by automated GitHub Actions CI,

39
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:26,000
and ready for deployment on IBM Quantum, Rigetti, or Amazon Braket quantum processors via our decoupled backend architecture.

40
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
We have published our complete open-source codebase, full documentation, and pre-trained checkpoints under the MIT License.

41
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Thank you.
